\tag{fdip}
\title{A dynamical connection and its matter law}
\date{2026-11-01}

\p{The [determinant action](fdip-0070) is a function of a fixed
connection. A measure on connections turns that function into part
of a joint law: one may first draw a connection and then draw a
Gaussian matter field in it. Integrating over the matter changes the
connection's probability, while conditioning on a connection recovers
the background Gaussian law.}

\p{A small square torus makes this distinction explicit. Its gauge
orbits reduce the calculation to a finite sum of positive determinant
weights. At zero bare gauge coupling, scalar matter already changes
the plaquette expectation from zero to a strictly positive number.
This finite comparison does not determine large-loop screening or an
infinite-volume area law.}

